	<div id="main"><h1>Governor's Executive Orders 2011</h1>
<div id="navcontainer">
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_001">Executive Order 11-01</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe winter weather that began on December 30, 2010. (Jan. 4)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_002">Executive Order 11-02</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon extends <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2010/eo10_027">Executive Order 10-27</a> and <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_001">Executive Order 11-01</a> through February 28, 2011. (Jan. 28)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_003">Executive Order 11-03</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon declares a State of Emergency and directs the State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe weather than began on January 31, 2011. (Jan. 31)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_004">Executive Order 11-04</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to severe weather that began on January 31, 2011. (Jan. 31)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_005">Executive Order 11-05</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Missouri Department of Transportation to assist counties in clearing snow due to the historic winter storm that began on January 31, 2011. (Feb. 4)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_006">Executive Order 11-06</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated in response to severe weather that began on April 22, 2011. (Apr. 22)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_007">Executive Order 11-07</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Director of the Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on April 22, 2011. (Apr. 25)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_008">Executive Order 11-08</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to severe weather that began on April 22, 2011. (Apr. 25)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_009">Executive Order 11-09</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon extends the declaration of emergency contained in <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_006">Executive Order 11-06</a> and the terms of Executive Orders <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_007">11-07</a> and <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_008">11-08</a> through June 20, 2011. (May 20)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_010"> Executive Order 11-10</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Missouri Department of Health and Senior Services and the State Board of Pharmacy vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to the tornado and severe storm aftermath in Joplin. (May 24)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_011"> Executive Order 11-11</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Director of Revenue to issue duplicate or replacement driver license, nondriver license, certificate of motor vehicle ownership, number plate, or tabs lost or destroyed as a result of the tornado that hit the city of Joplin and to waive all state fees and charges for such duplicate or replacement. (May 26)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_012"> Executive Order 11-12</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders the Director of the Department of Insurance, Financial Institutions, and Professional Registration to temporarily waive, suspend, and/or modify any statute or regulation under his purview in order to best serve the interests of those citizens affected by the tornado and severe storm aftermath in Jasper and Newton County. (May 26)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_013"> Executive Order 11-13</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon authorizes the Joplin Public School system to immediately begin rebuilding and replacing the materials for three of its buildings that were destroyed in a tornado that struck on May 22, 2011, without requiring advertisement for bids. (May 26)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_014"> Executive Order 11-14</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to a tornado that hit the City of Joplin on May 22, 2011. (May 26)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_015"> Executive Order 11-15</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon authorizes the Joplin Public School system to immediately rebuild, restore, and/or renovate their buildings that were damaged by a tornado and severe storms on May 22, 2011, without requiring advertisement for bids. (June 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_016"> Executive Order 11-16</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon authorizes the Joplin Public School system to immediately begin to retrofit and furnish warehouse and retail structures to house district programs displaced by the tornado and severe storms on May 22, 2011, without requiring advertisement for bids. (June 3)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_017"> Executive Order 11-17</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon establishes the State of Missouri Resource, Recovery & Rebuilding Center in the City of Joplin in response to the tornado and severe storms on May 22, 2011. (June 7)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_018"> Executive Order 11-18</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon orders and directs the Adjutant General to coordinate and supervise efforts to prepare and respond to flooding events occurring and threatened along the Missouri River and tributaries and to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities. (June 8)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_019"> Executive Order 11-19</a></strong><br>Gov. Nixon extends Executive Orders <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_006">11-06</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_007">11-07</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_008">11-08</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_010">11-10</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_011">11-11</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_013">11-13</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_014">11-14</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_015">11-15</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_016">11-16</a>, and <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_018">11-18</a> until September 15, 2011. (June 17)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_020"> Executive Order 11-20</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon extends certain terms of <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_012">Executive Order 11-12</a> to assist Missouri citizens impacted by the tornado and severe storms in the city of Joplin on May 22, 2011. (June 17)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_021"> Executive Order 11-21</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon authorizes the Joplin Public School system to immediately begin to retrofit, equip, and furnish various buildings to house students during the 2011-12 school year without requiring advertisement for bids. (June 17)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_022"> Executive Order 11-22</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (July 26)<strong></strong></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_023"> Executive Order 11-23</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon extends <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_020">Executive Order 11-20</a> until October 15, 2011, and extends Executive Orders <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_006">11-06</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_007">11-07</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_008">11-08</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_011">11-11</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_014">11-14</a>, and <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_018">11-18</a> until December 15, 2011. (Sep. 13)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_024"> Executive Order 11-24</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Nov. 18)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_025"> Executive Order 11-25</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon extends the declaration of emergency contained in <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_006">Executive Order 11-06</a>, and extends Executive Orders <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_007">11-07</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_011">11-11</a> and <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2011/eo11_014">11-14</a> until March 15, 2012. (Dec. 14)</p>
